C SUBSET - ERROR RECOVERY AND COMPILER DIAGNOSTICS

READ /man/languages/c FIRST. cc is a small source-to-Thumb compiler,
NOT gcc, and has no linker, headers or general libc calls.

COMPLETE TOOLCHAIN
  write_file('/tmp/t.c', 'int main(){write(1,"OK\n",3);return 0;}')
  cc /tmp/t.c
  cat /tmp/t.s
  as /tmp/t.s
  /tmp/a.out
The output assembly path is derived from the C source filename.
The assembler always writes /tmp/a.out, replacing the previous one.

LIMITS OF PARTICULAR IMPORTANCE
  C source <=1024 B; assembly <=4096 B but as input <=2048 B.
  Function count <=16; function parameters <=4.
  Local variable count <=16; frame <=256 B per function.
  Array dimensions one, lengths 1..64; no globals.
  No #include, preprocessors, printf, malloc, stdio/stdlib,
  struct, typedef, switch, for, ++, compound assignments.
  No implicit arbitrary function declarations or general libraries.

COMMON FAILURE PATTERNS
  cc rejects: unsupported token, too many vars/funcs, output too
    large, unsupported expression or source too long.
  as rejects: unsupported instruction, branch out of Thumb-1
    range, wrong mnemonic, operand/offset wrong, source >2048.
  runtime exits unexpectedly: invalid pointer, local stack frame,
    read/write error or incorrect pointer arithmetic.
  unexpected output: verify write count includes exact bytes.

ISOLATE BEFORE REWRITING
  1) create a minimal hello with main + write.
  2) run cc, read generated assembly.
  3) run as and run /tmp/a.out.
  4) add one feature at a time, keep source short.
  5) use trace on -s / trace show for syscalls when needed.

C GENERATED BY cc IS POSITION INDEPENDENT BY DESIGN, but raw
absolute data addresses in manually written assembler are not.
Do not assume cc implements ANSI C's undefined behavior checks.

If cc reports 'generated assembly exceeds RAM file limit', simplify
code generation; the 2048-byte .s file cannot be saved. This is NOT
a 1024-byte C source-size error or evidence of unsupported syntax.
If 'cannot create assembly file', inspect /proc/ramfiles for an
11-entry table full condition; do not delete unknown files.
